  "decision_summary": "L3 oral exposure records do not change the prior high prediction: verapamil exposure records (C166, C162) are consistent with oral absorption but are not direct F evidence, and most L3 records are for unrelated molecules. The closest analog verapamil has F 22% fasted and 34-49% SR, and sulfonyl-containing analogs sulpiride/levosulpiride have F 23-35%, all above 20%. No affirmative threshold-relevant evidence supports F < 20%. Prediction: high, moderate confidence."
}

